# Series Narrative Architecture Rule

When planning content cards, default to a **series arc**, not a single
standalone thesis card, especially during the first 1–3 months of an account
or when introducing a new technical theme.

This rule is derived from the Threads breakout case study of
`@10m.engineer.investor`. See
[research/swipe/2026-05-15_threads-breakout-10m-engineer-investor_deep-dive.md](mdc:research/swipe/2026-05-15_threads-breakout-10m-engineer-investor_deep-dive.md).

Use this together with
[.cursor/rules/content-voice-raw-research.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/content-voice-raw-research.mdc).
Voice rules still apply on top of structure rules.

## When To Apply

Apply this rule when ANY of the following is true:

- Account is in its first 3 months of active publishing.
- Topic requires domain knowledge a general reader does not yet have.
- Thesis depends on multiple layers of evidence the audience has not seen.
- Card is the first in a planned thread of related cards.

## When NOT To Apply

Skip when ALL of the following are true:

- Account already has months of established explainer content for this theme.
- Audience is professional and the technical foundation is assumed.
- Content is time-sensitive news commentary that cannot wait for an arc.

If you skip, write the reason inline in the card frontmatter under
`series_arc_skipped: <reason>`.

## Required Structure: Three-Phase Arc

A series should plan three phases. A card belongs to exactly one phase.

### Phase 1 — Explainer (Episodes 1–3 typically)

- No ticker. No company name. No buy / sell signal.
- Goal: build the reader's mental model of the topic.
- Voice: "我們一起看", not "你應該知道".
- Hook: familiar cross-domain analogy + small surprise.
- End each episode with a tease for the next episode.

### Phase 2 — Mechanism (Episodes 4–6 typically)

- Introduce components / supply chain / cash flow without yet recommending.
- Name companies only where they are structurally unavoidable.
- Reader should now be able to explain the topic to a friend.

### Phase 3 — Thesis (Episodes 7+)

- Investment view, with position disclosure if any.
- Lead with the counter / invalidation, not the buy case.
- Allowed only after Phase 1 and Phase 2 have shipped.

A card that skips directly from Phase 1 to Phase 3 violates this rule.

## Hook Requirement (Phase 1 Episode 1)

Episode 1 must use a **familiar mental model + small surprise** hook, not a
raw number. Pattern:

```text
<reader-familiar object>
→ <unexpected comparison to the topic>
→ <one sentence on why this matters>
```

Worked examples that satisfy the rule:

- `傳統位元 = 開關 → 量子位元 = 30%/70% 概率 → 一個位元就代表兩個可能性`
  (from the case study)
- `為什麼一台 AI server 一個月電費比一台 Model S 還貴 → rack 是住在大樓裡的小型發電廠 → 熱密度問題`
  (Card #001 candidate)

Hooks that violate the rule (Phase 1):

- `GB300 一櫃液冷 BOM 接近 $50K` (number-first, no analogy, presumes
  investment frame).
- `奇鋐 / 雙鴻 / Vertiv 是這波受惠標的` (ticker-first).

## Format Defaults For Threads

- Long-form content posts as **numbered posts in a single thread**, not as
  outer post + collapsed text attachment. Each numbered post must be
  independently readable, likeable, repostable.
- Series header lives in the first post: `【散熱系列：第一集 - 標題】`.
- Outer post for Episode 1 ≤ 280 characters, ends in a question or tease.

For X, single long post is acceptable; the series identity still goes in the
opening line.

## Link Placement Policy

Threads and X both downrank posts containing outbound links. Apply a
**phased policy** based on account traction.

| Phase | Trigger | Link policy |
|---|---|---|
| early | < 1K followers OR first series in progress | **No outbound link** in main post or first reply. Bio link also off. Pure native content. |
| mid | 1K–5K followers AND ≥ 1 series fully shipped | Link in **first reply only**, never main post. Bio link allowed. |
| late | > 5K followers OR specific monetization goal | Link in main post acceptable for thesis episodes (Phase 3) only. Explainer (Phase 1) still link-free. |

Default for any new account is **early**. Promotion between phases requires
an explicit decision in `ops/decisions/`. Do not assume the next phase based
on a single viral post.

Anti-pattern: pasting a link in the main post of an early-phase explainer
because "the reader needs to know where to go for more". Early readers
follow the profile, they do not click external links. Link click-through
on an early account is statistically near zero AND costs you reach.

## Voice And Disclosure

- Phase 1 episodes have no position disclosure because there is no claim to
  disclose.
- Phase 3 episodes must include position disclosure per the existing rule
  in [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md).
- Counter / invalidation framing in Phase 3 must come **before** any
  bullish synthesis.

## Frontmatter Fields

When a card belongs to a series, the markdown frontmatter must include:

```yaml
series: <series-slug>          # e.g. "ai-server-thermal"
series_episode: <integer>      # 1, 2, 3, ...
series_phase: explainer | mechanism | thesis
series_arc_total: <integer or null>   # planned total, null if open-ended
series_prereq_episodes: [<episode numbers>]  # which episodes must ship first
```

A card with `series_phase: thesis` must not have `public_status: ready`
until at least one `series_phase: explainer` episode is `public_status: ready`.

## Anti-Patterns

- Writing the thesis card first, then back-filling explainers. Always plan
  arc top-down before drafting any single episode.
- Using "第一集" without a numbered plan for at least episodes 2 and 3.
- Burying the counter inside the bullish argument in Phase 3.
- Using one rich analogy in Episode 1 and then dropping into pure jargon by
  Episode 2.

